<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shalmaneser III</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 859–824 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century-bce">9th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shalmaneser III was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assyrian-empire">Assyria</a> from 859 to 824 BCE. He campaigned almost every year, annexing Bit-Adini on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/euphrates">Euphrates</a>, fighting a coalition of Syrian and Levantine kings at Qarqar in 853 BCE, and taking tribute from Israel, as shown on his Black <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/obelisk">Obelisk</a>. His wars also reached Urartu, Que in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cilicia">Cilicia</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zagros-mountains">Zagros</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chaldean-tribes">Chaldean tribes</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylonia">Babylonia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/shalmaneser-iii.jpg" alt="Shalmaneser III" width="320" height="616" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Osama Shukir Muhammed Amin FRCP(Glasg) · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Shalmaneser_III_(relief_detail).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
